      "Reason": "Loads raw eBPF instructions supplied in memory rather than an ELF object. Native execution requires a module that bpf2c compiled ahead of time from an ELF object, so this API surface has no native artifact by construction."
    },
    {
      "Executable": "unit_tests.exe",
      "Test": "trampoline_test",
      "Reason": "Exercises the trampoline table, which is the indirect helper dispatch mechanism used by JIT compiled programs. Native modules bind their helpers at build time and never allocate a trampoline table."
    },
    {
      "Executable": "unit_tests.exe",
      "Test": "valid bpf_load_program with map-jit",
